* text=auto
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Test fixtures are checked in VERBATIM — they are third-party files a test reads
# back and compares against measured counts. `* text=auto` above would normalise
# them on commit and hand this box CRLF on checkout, so the bytes on disk would
# not be the bytes that were copied in (courtroom_fonts.ini has no trailing
# newline, which is part of the fixture).
internal/ui/testdata/** -text
# Same rule, same reason: the theme-format fixtures are hand-authored files a
# test parses and re-emits byte-for-byte, down to the column alignment, the
# percent escapes and the trailing newline. `* text=auto` would rewrite them on
# commit and hand this box back different bytes on checkout, which would turn a
# statement about the writer into a statement about the checkout. (The CRLF /
# no-final-newline shape most of the real corpus is in is deliberately NOT
# checked in — TestASidecarWithWindowsLineEndingsRoundTrips builds it in Go, for
# exactly that reason.)
internal/theme/testdata/** -text
